ierarchy stops at ServiceID, so the deployment_id itself is not a scope leg), so project-, environment-, and service-scoped grants are denied at the boundary by the engine's covers() rule (a grant with a pinned ProjectID cannot cover a resource with no ProjectID); principals whose only access is a scoped grant must use a parent-scoped route family to address a deployment by its (project, environment, service, deployment) tuple. A cross-tenant or unknown deployment_id reaches the persistence layer with the principal's home organization id and is rejected as a deterministic 404 by the tenant-scoped repository query, never disguised as a 200 with another tenant's data and never as a 403 that would confirm existence.",
