 ## Codebase Patterns
+- Build/deployment metering is a bridge from Yalla source-of-truth timelines into append-only `usage_events`: deployment counts come from terminal `deployment_events` (never Dokploy current state), successful/rolled-back deployments use `deployments`, failed deployments use `failed_deployments`, cancelled deployments do not emit deployment-count usage, and `build_minutes` sums completed `job_attempts` durations with a terminal `provisioning_jobs.started_at/finished_at` fallback. Idempotency keys are per deployment outcome (`deployment:<id>:<status>`) and per job duration (`build_minutes:<job_id>`).
 - Traefik metric attribution is a separate layer after source collection: extract explicit Yalla service labels before deterministic Dokploy/Traefik names containing `svc_<id>`/`svc-<id>`, resolve only services that still have a service-level `dokploy_refs` mapping, attach full org/project/environment/service scope plus attribution source/confidence metadata, and quarantine missing-ref, deleted-service, and unmanaged samples so they never become billing-grade `usage_events` automatically.
 - Traefik metering source collection lives under `internal/controlplane/metering` and should stay source-only: query bounded Prometheus windows, normalize counters into deterministic unattributed samples, attach `query_version` plus raw-sample checksum metadata, and leave tenant attribution/quarantine plus `usage_events` writes to later attribution/aggregation layers.
 - Billing-period usage counters are replayed from append-only `usage_events` through `store.UsageCounterRepository.AggregateUsageEvents`: open periods upsert deterministic `(organization_id, key, unit, period_start, period_end, source)` counters, while previously closed counters keep their frozen quantity and record net-new late-arriving usage in `usage_counter_adjustments` so replays are idempotent and invoice adjustments stay auditable.

