+  - Postgres-backed metering tests use `testutil.RequireMigratedDB`; they require no live Dokploy server.
+- Remaining risks or follow-ups
+  - The emitter is a store-backed bridge; a later worker/scheduler story still needs to decide when to call it during deployment job settlement or replay.
+  - Future metric-definition/backoffice stories should expose these new usage resources through their configuration surfaces.
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - Deployment metering must read terminal `deployment_events` before emitting deployment-count usage so billing never infers customer deploys from mutable Dokploy current state.
+  - Retry build time should sum immutable `job_attempts`; cancelled attempts still contribute elapsed worker time, but cancelled deployments should not consume the successful/failed deployment-count entitlement key.
+  - Adding a quota/usage resource requires both the Go `QuotaResource` closed set and a new `ALTER DOMAIN quota_resource` migration; `TestQuotaResourceValid` pins the Go-side lockstep count.
